{"type":"standard","title":"Randy Villegas","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Randy Villegas</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q139551327","titles":{"canonical":"Randy_Villegas","normalized":"Randy Villegas","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Randy Villegas</span></span>"},"pageid":80034639,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Randy_Villegas_at_Vota_Palooza_in_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Randy_Villegas_at_Vota_Palooza_in_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":439},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/Randy_Villegas_at_Vota_Palooza_in_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":814,"height":1084},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378809024","tid":"7635250b-c14e-11f1-9bfd-46be48787a02","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:23:36Z","description":"American educator and politician (born 1994)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Villegas","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Villegas?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Villegas?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Randy_Villegas"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Villegas","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Randy_Villegas","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Villegas?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Randy_Villegas"}},"extract":"Randy Villegas is an American professor, businessman, and politician. Villegas is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 election for California's 22nd congressional district, which encompasses the southern Central Valley. In California's June 2026 top-two primary, he finished ahead of Democratic state assemblymember Jasmeet Bains and advanced to the general election against Republican incumbent David Valadao. Villegas works as a professor at the College of the Sequoias.","extract_html":"<p><b>Randy Villegas</b> is an American professor, businessman, and politician. Villegas is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 election for California's 22nd congressional district, which encompasses the southern Central Valley. In California's June 2026 top-two primary, he finished ahead of Democratic state assemblymember Jasmeet Bains and advanced to the general election against Republican incumbent David Valadao. Villegas works as a professor at the College of the Sequoias.</p>"}